_update_caches() {
  if command -v gtk-update-icon-cache >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    gtk-update-icon-cache -q -t -f /usr/share/icons/hicolor 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
  if command -v update-desktop-database >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    update-desktop-database -q /usr/share/applications 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
}

_print_init_help() {
  cat <<'EOF'

Lumo Desktop is installed. It starts in the tray; use the tray icon or the
global shortcut to open it.

To start Lumo automatically at login, either enable "Launch at startup" in
Lumo's settings (this uses XDG autostart and works on every init system), or
use the service that matches your init system:

  systemd:
    systemctl --user daemon-reload
    systemctl --user enable --now lumo-desktop.service

  OpenRC (Artix):
    rc-update --user add lumo-desktop default
    rc-service --user lumo-desktop start

OpenRC user services require a user OpenRC session (Artix's openrc-user PAM
integration) and the Artix dbus-openrc package (plus elogind-openrc if you use
elogind). If that is not set up, use the XDG autostart setting instead.

Updates are handled by pacman, not Lumo's built-in updater.
EOF
}

post_install() {
  _update_caches
  _print_init_help
}

post_upgrade() {
  _update_caches
  _print_init_help
}

post_remove() {
  _update_caches
}
